|Spain
|Soup made of raw vegetables and served cold, usually with a tomato base, originating in the southern Spanish region of Andalusia.|In Andalusia, most gazpacho recipes typically include stale bread, tomato, cucumber, bell pepper, onion and garlic, olive oil, wine vinegar, water, and salt.
